Constellation Mapper
====================

Write a function:

    def constellation_mapper(stars: list[tuple[int, int]], size: int) -> list[str]

Build a size x size grid of '.' characters and mark every star with '*'.
Each star is a (row, col) tuple; stars outside the grid are ignored.
Return the grid as a list of strings, one string per row.

Examples:
    constellation_mapper([(0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 2)], 3) -> ['*..', '.*.', '..*']
    constellation_mapper([(1, 1), (0, 1), (2, 1), (1, 0), (1, 2)], 3) -> ['.*.', '***', '.*.']
    constellation_mapper([], 2) -> ['..', '..']
    constellation_mapper([(0, 0), (5, 5)], 3) -> ['*..', '...', '...']
    constellation_mapper([(0, 1), (1, 1), (2, 1)], 3) -> ['.*.', '.*.', '.*.']
